# in which languages are string immutable

Strings are immutable in many popular programming languages, including:

Python
Java   
C#   
JavaScript   
Go   
In these languages, once a string object is created, its value cannot be changed directly. This means that any operation that appears to modify a string actually creates a new string object with the modified value.   

This immutability has several advantages:   

Thread Safety: Immutable strings can be safely shared among multiple threads without the risk of data corruption.   
Caching: Immutable strings can be easily cached, as their values never change.   
Security: Immutable strings can help prevent unintended modifications to sensitive data.   
While immutability might seem restrictive at first, it provides a solid foundation for efficient and safe string manipulation in these languages.


